+## Build / run
+- Build ONLY from `fyp_jaspr_web`: `env -u HTTP_PROXY -u HTTPS_PROXY -u http_proxy -u https_proxy dart run jaspr_cli:jaspr build`. Deletes `build/jaspr` → stop servers first. Stale build_runner: kill `dart.exe` + `rm .dart_tool/build/asset_graph.json`. Auth-bridge edits: `cd tool && npm run build-auth` first.
+- SPA is client-rendered; deep routes via `lib/app.dart` redirect. Serve `PORT=8090 node tool/dev_static_server.js`. Headless probes: chromium `--no-proxy-server`, NODE_PATH=`C:/Users/Lenovo/.workbuddy-ai/binaries/node/workspace/node_modules`.
+- Ports: 8090 web / 8000 API (`sitewise.main:app`) / 5567 dev proxy / 8181 VM / 5432 PG. `FYP/test` (3001) is legacy — never the API. A uvicorn `--reload` on 8090 is a misport: kill parent **and** the orphaned `multiprocessing.spawn` child.
+- `.\serve` → serve.cmd → serve.impl.ps1. NEVER create `serve.ps1` (AllSigned rejects unsigned).
+
+## Test isolation (hard rule)
+- Direct `pytest` is refused by the guard (`TEST ISOLATION REFUSED … Final_Location_Analysis@5432`). Always `tools/p2_isolated_test_runner_20261122.py --db project1_disposable_app`. JUnit: replicate runner inline, add `--junitxml`.
+- Any authenticated `/auth/me` on the :8090 backend **writes a `public.users` row** into the protected DB via `get_or_sync_current` (happened once; reversed). Verify DB identity before the first authenticated request.
+
+## Supabase auth
+- **18 auth users exist** (owner's test accounts) — never modify an existing one. Signup returns 200 with **no token** (email confirmation). Admin confirm `PUT /auth/v1/admin/users/{id}` `{email_confirm:true}` + password grant → genuine ES256 JWT. `DELETE` fails on FK `role_change_audit_user_id_affected_fkey` → ban instead.
+- `/api/v1/auth/me` returns `full_name: ""` for fresh accounts; `??` falls back only on null, so `substring(0,1)` throws. Guard blanks.
+
+## Jaspr gotchas
+- Never root a 3rd-party widget on a framework element (Jaspr rewrites `class`). Component asset refs must be root-absolute `/assets/...`.
+- `@client` components accept ONLY primitive params — pass raw JSON strings, parse inside.
+- Status cells mix Icon + label spans; read the LAST `span`.
+
+## Registry discipline (`q01-q13-explanation/1`)
+- Generated by `backend/scripts/build_explanation_registry.py` → `deliverables/…REGISTRY.json` **and** runtime copy `src/sitewise/project1/data/`. Never hand-edit. `EXPECTED_REGISTRY_SHA256` pinned in `project1/explanation_registry.py`; regenerating without updating the pin 503s everything.
+- `data/` has no `__init__.py`; JSON loads via `Path(__file__).with_name('data')`.
+- Conflict status (CX-17/CX-19 encoding, ordinal provenance) is **computed** from the file each build, so records can't outlive defects.
+- Chart contract `chart-spec/1`: `percentage` = Decimal serialized as JSON **string**; bars render only at `render_state == RENDERABLE`, which stays unreachable until an A10 admission adapter is adopted. `ChartSpec.evidence_context_hash` is the chart↔explanation join key.
